{
  "dom_id": "step-15721",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors Using Angle Bracket Notation",
  "problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -7, 15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 14, -11 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$.",
  "worked_solution": "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b},$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-3b & =⟨-7,15⟩-3\\cdot ⟨14,-11⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,15⟩-⟨42,-33⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7-42,15-(-33)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-49,48⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
